  "working_thesis": "Hannah Arendt's 'The Human Condition' provides a foundational phenomenological analysis of the vita activa (labor, work, and action) and examines how the modern rise of the 'social' realm has transformed the public and private spheres, threatening human plurality and the durable common world."
